meta {
  name: List Manga Chapters
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/manga/:id/chapters?filter=all
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  id: one-piece.49
}

params:query {
  filter: all
}

assert {
  res.status: in [200, 404]
}

docs {
  # List Manga Chapters
  Returns the complete list of chapters for a manga, annotated with local CBZ archive download status (`downloaded: true/false`).

  > **Note**: Unlike older versions of iFetch, calling this endpoint **does not** trigger automatic background downloads. To download chapters, use `POST /api/manga/:id/download`.

  ### Path Parameters
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  |-----------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `id` | string | **Yes** | Manga Katana slug identifier (e.g. `one-piece.49`). |

  ### Query Parameters
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Default | Allowed Values | Description |
  |-----------|------|----------|---------|----------------|-------------|
  | `filter` | string | No | `all` | `all`, `downloaded`, `missing` | Filters the returned chapter list by download status. |

  ### Responses
  - **`200 OK`**: JSON array of chapters.
    ```json
    [
      {
        "number": "1",
        "title": "Romance Dawn",
        "url": "https://mangakatana.com/manga/one-piece.49/c1",
        "downloaded": true
      },
      {
        "number": "2",
        "title": "They Call Him 'Straw Hat Luffy'",
        "url": "https://mangakatana.com/manga/one-piece.49/c2",
        "downloaded": false
      }
    ]
    ```
  - **`400 Bad Request`**: If `id` or `filter` query parameter is invalid.
}
